It's exact value can be described as 
$$
e = 1 + 1 + \frac{1}{1*2} + \frac{1}{1*2*3} + \frac{1}{1*2*3*4} + \frac{1}{1*2*3*4*5} + ... 
$$


Like any other number, $e$ follows normal power properties:

$$
\begin{align}
e^{x+y}&=&e^x\cdot e^y \\
e^{-x}&=&\frac{1}{e^x}\\
e^{x-y}&=&\frac{e^x}{e^y}\\
e^{rx}&=&(e^x)^r 
\end{align}
$$

